      "answer": "No stored context on this locker yet — here's a general-purpose layout you can adapt. I've used your code as the address prefix so the scheme stays consistent if you ever add more lockers (e.g. LOCKER-90D3F2 → LOCKER-41C7B1).\n\n##1. Core principle\n**Zone by access frequency, not by category of object.** People lose things in storage because everything ends up in one \"misc\" pile. Sort by *how often you'll need it*, and let the physical position do the remembering.\n\n## 2. Zone map (assume a ~2–3 m wide unit)\n\n```\n        ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n        │ back wall: tall / flat items │  ← upright, rarely touched\n        │  art boards, frames, suitcases│\n        │ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐        │\n DOOR →│ │ 01     │ │ 02     │        │  ← FRONT ZONE: daily/weekly\n        │ │ DAILY  │ │ ACTIVE │        │\n        │ └────────┘ └────────┘        │\n        │ shelf 2: 03 04 05 06  (household / tools)\n        │ shelf 3: 07 08 09  (seasonal, lidded bins)\n        │ shelf 4: 10 11     (archive"
    },
    "ask_first": {
      "session_id": "a7a297d4-0b05-4107-8109-0f161861c5ee",
